      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `JsonAutoDetectTest_testFactoryMethods.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/jackson-annotations/manual/testcases/JsonAutoDetectTest/JsonAutoDetectTest_testFactoryMethods.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved version with better understandability — splitting into focused test methods with descriptive names and clearer structure.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version splits the original single test method into two focused, descriptively-named tests — one verifying that targeting a single accessor (`FIELD`) leaves all others at `DEFAULT`, and one verifying that `ALL` sets every accessor to the specified visibility — with assertion messages that make each check self-documenting."
    }
